KZ2 patch 6061: cellFont outline API on the bundled Noto Sans for the system fontsets (issue #39).

From Project Helghast port/patches/5005-cellfont-outline-fontset.patch (the Killzone 3 PC port "Project Helghast", same
author, MIT), adapted: new libs/font/cellFontOutline.c with cellFontGetCharGlyphMetrics (NID 0xD8EAEE9F),
cellFontGenerateCharGlyph (0xC17259DE), cellFontDeleteGlyph (0xD62F5D76) and cellFontEndLibrary (0x40D40544), which
ps3recomp did not define: Killzone 2's imports took the unresolved-NID path (CELL_OK, out-parameters untouched), so
every character its three Latin-only embedded fonts lack (Cyrillic, Greek) was blank. Kept from 5005: the font chain
per fontset handle with a cmap lookup per code point, the outline conversion (stb_truetype shapes; cubics split into
quadratics), the guest record layout, the size-class pool, and a context handler for cellFontSetScalePixel and
cellFontSetupRenderScalePixel that reads w and h from f1/f2 (the flat adapter passes r3..r10 only, so the flat entry
stored the host's stale xmm1/xmm2). Changed for KZ2, after an earlier change's contract (the RE notes):
- fonts: NotoSans-Regular.ttf from $KZ2_FONT_DIR, else <exe dir>/fonts, else ./fonts (tools/runtime/mkfont_noto.py
  makes it from nixpkgs' noto-fonts; never committed); no firmware fonts, no CJK files; Windows paths are wide (UTF-8
  inside), so an install path with Cyrillic letters works;
- a code no font has, and code 0: CELL_FONT_ERROR_NO_SUPPORT_CODE 0x80540011 with *glyph = 0 (5005: CELL_OK and an
  empty half-em glyph; KZ2 then falls back to its own blank entry, @0x0004190C); an unopened font: 0x80540002; before
  cellFontInit: UNINITIALIZED; no success ever returns a null record;
- the pool is the file cache the title passes to cellFontInit (CellFontConfig.FileCache, KZ2: 0x40000 bytes of its BSS
  at 0x011B0EB8), which cellFont.c now records (cellFontInit logs it); 5005 used KZ3's allocation window (KZ3 patch
  1113, not in KZ2). cellFontDeleteGlyph refuses a pointer it did not hand out.
Also needed (port/kz2/hle_kz2.cpp, same round): KZ2's own context handler for cellFontInitializeWithRevision returned 0
without calling cellFontInit, so cellFontOpenFontset failed with UNINITIALIZED and the game gave up on the system font
for good; it is removed and the runtime's flat cellFontInitializeWithRevision -> cellFontInit runs.
An earlier change (D53): a second file in the chain, NotoSansCJK-Regular.ttc (tools/runtime/mkfont_cjk.py: Noto Sans CJK, OFL
1.1, a static Regular instance with TrueType outlines cut to the characters of the game's own text), so Japanese,
Korean and Chinese text is no longer blank; a collection's faces are all loaded (stb_truetype offsets per index) and
the face is picked per lookup by the weak kz2_cjk_face_index() (port/kz2/kz2_cjk_face.cpp: the game's page language),
so Han characters get their language's shapes (0 JP, 1 KR, 2 SC, 3 TC, 4 HK); .ttc is a searched extension.
Host test: tools/runtime/test_font_fallback.sh. Upstream candidate (general: the outline API, a fontset backed by real
files, SetScalePixel's float arguments, the file cache as the record pool).

